Title: Minimum Jumps Calculator

Main goal: The function computes a piecewise estimate of the minimum number of jumps needed for a target distance, given two jump lengths. It first orders the two jump lengths so the first is the smaller and the second is the larger. It then returns:
- the ceiling of the target divided by the larger jump when the target is greater than or equal to the larger jump;
- 0 if the target is 0;
- 1 if the target equals the smaller jump;
- 2 in all other cases.
